  "foaf:name": "Southern Gulf of Guinea Upwelling System",
  "sdo:name": "Southern Gulf of Guinea Upwelling System",
  "sdo:description": "The Southern Gulf of Guinea Upwelling System (sGGUS) is a key area of marine productivity in the eastern tropical Atlantic, yet its response to climate change remains poorly understood. Under climate warming, the rising sea surface temperatures and increased freshwater discharge could intensify stratification, affect upwelling efficiency and nutrient availability, and potentially threaten fisheries-dependent communities in the region. This project will use a climate projection model to evaluate the potential impact of future changes on the sGGUS. A comparative analysis with other systems will provide insights for sustainable fisheries and climate resilience strategies. Throughout the project, capacity-building initiatives related to coastal observation management and climate modeling will be implemented for early-career scientists and students specializing in relevant marine science disciplines.",
  "sdo:location": "Congo",
  "sdo:identifier": "34.8",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/southern-gulf-of-guinea-upwelling-system/",
